      "problem": "$7-\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{4}}+6t\\sqrt[3]{2t}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{4}}+6t\\sqrt[3]{2t} & = \\\\ 7-\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}\\cdot 2t}+6t\\sqrt[3]{2t} & = \\\\ 7-\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{2t}+6t\\sqrt[3]{2t} & = \\\\ 7-t\\sqrt[3]{2t}+6t\\sqrt[3]{2t} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-t\\sqrt[3]{2t}+6t\\sqrt[3]{2t} & = \\\\ 7+(-t+6t)\\sqrt[3]{2t} & = \\\\ 7+5t\\sqrt[3]{2t} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
